rect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b1d"], "question": {"text": "The reverse break down voltage of a Zener diode is <math><mn>5.6</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> in the given circuit.<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F2f0d43af-5654-4e27-898f-2898c8c61476-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 119px;\" /><br />The current <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></math> through the Zener is:"}, "options": [{"id": "f73e1f", "text": "<math><mi> </mi><mn>10</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cc3"}, {"id": "ded1f9", "text": "<math><mi> </mi><mn>7</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cc4"}, {"id": "048fb0", "text": "<math><mn>17</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cc5"}, {"id": "1a320b", "text": "<math><mn>15</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cc6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cc7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9942"], "question": {"text": "Boolean relation at the output stage- <math><mi>Y</mi></math> for the following circuit is:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F41c8f060-4da1-4123-8afe-e20c1382b9ef.jpeg?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "053f6d", "text": "<math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>-</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>-</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cc8"}, {"id": "bc801a", "text": "<math><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cc9"}, {"id": "e86015", "text": "<math><mi>A</mi><mo>∙</mo><mi>B</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cca"}, {"id": "0d0a3c", "text": "<math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>-</mo></mover><mo>∙</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>-</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ccb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ccc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b470c"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the given circuit the input voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub></math> is shown in figure. The cut-in voltage of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></math> junction diode (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>) is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. Which of the following output voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced></math> waveform across the diode is correct?</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F5d75a0e0-485c-4ea1-972d-5e4d5fa8257f-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 560px; height: 142px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d34d00", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F70a53c50-18fb-4f37-9359-3dbc92da8e46-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 102px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ccd"}, {"id": "dcbf7c", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F28885ab6-65bf-4bb7-8b75-e860075a04c0-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 103px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cce"}, {"id": "3df692", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F267cea6a-e040-48b4-b672-d278ff042f0a-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 210px; height: 113px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ccf"}, {"id": "f6c249", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F200f306b-f17a-4240-8f7e-0caf63d3fafc-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 210px; height: 112px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cd0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cd1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb7"], "question": {"text": "<p>The logic gate equivalent to the given circuit diagram is :</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F2fc50d1d-7921-44bb-b9a1-436b9d03de9c-9893962.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 283px; height: 330px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "247593", "text": "OR", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cd2"}, {"id": "2f4a0f", "text": "NAND", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4