 "text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff65f0750-f00a-4c3c-8aa1-a428ae0390e0-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 85px;\" /></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cdf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ce0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b1d"], "question": {"text": "In the given circuit the current through Zener Diode is close to:\n\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fxs8EATWKrwPcXPpnn33fMrwL7_F2gu8bO8wZY_Tmcdw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">"}, "options": [{"id": "7aa545", "text": "$0.0 \\mathrm{~mA}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ce1"}, {"id": "86f6dc", "text": "$6.7 \\mathrm{~mA}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ce2"}, {"id": "edf27d", "text": "$4.0 \\mathrm{~mA}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ce3"}, {"id": "3d1fb9", "text": "$6.0 \\mathrm{~mA}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ce4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ce5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9942"], "question": {"text": "The output $\\mathrm{Y}$ of following circuit for given inputs is :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FKHTV-zcI1mTIEc9jyq-I0MjXCooKl0pUP1DS6uEJiT4.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "fc3fe3", "text": "$\\Lambda \\cdot B(\\Lambda+B)$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ce6"}, {"id": "3e5097", "text": "0", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ce7"}, {"id": "67c446", "text": "$\\overline{\\mathrm{A}} \\cdot \\mathrm{B}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ce8"}, {"id": "cc6941", "text": "$A \\cdot B$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ce9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cea", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b470c"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p><strong>Statement I</strong> : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;junction diodes can be used to function as a transistor, simply by connecting two diodes, back to back, which acts as the base terminal</p><p><strong>Statement II</strong>: In the study of transistors, the amplification factor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;indicates ratio of the collector current to the base current.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "fcbd73", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ceb"}, {"id": "d7aa97", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cec"}, {"id": "2903c7", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245ced"}, {"id": "40c63a", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cee"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f282ee0e063d9245cef", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb7"], "question": {"text": "<p>The output from a NAND gate having inputs A and B given below will be,</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.ap